Preserve given status when response body is null

Koa should preserve status to a greater extent, as it's replacing what the user added if certain situations happens (null/undefined body)


Suppose a basic app with no middlewares

```ts
app.use((ctx, next) => {
  ctx.status = 404;
});
```
This sets the body to the plain text "Not Found", however there's no need to place any redundancy, as 404 already implies that, and when there's no useful info to return it's better to omit the body completely. However if you explicitly set the body to null, koa changes the status to 204 automatically

```ts
app.use((ctx, next) => {
  ctx.status = 404;
  ctx.body  = null; // same case when setting ctx.body = undefined
});
```

Of course 204 is no expected response for a "not found" response, so the only way to proceed is sending a redundant body. I'm aware of #1421 but this is not the same case, I don't want to return null or 'null', there shouldn't be any body at all (like 204 does).

